"content":"`--rejudge`"},"516":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-82","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"Judge again even when the same request already has a judgment"},"517":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-83","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"`--ci`"},"518":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-84","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"CI mode: the suite passes when its pass rate meets the run's threshold"},"519":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-85","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"`--format <FORMAT>`"},"520":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-86","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"`table` or `json` only"},"521":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-87","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"`--json`"},"522":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-88","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"Shorthand for `--format json`"},"523":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-89","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"`--no-fail`"},"524":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-90","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"Exit zero on suite failure. Does **not** suppress a judge error"},"525":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-91","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"A judge is one native chat completion per trial — no agent, no tools, nothing injected that the judge's author did not write. Each exchange is recorded in full in `trial-N/judgments.json`, and the engine, never the model, computes every score from the reply."},"526":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-92","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"Rewrites are additive: `result.json`, `aggregated.json` and `summary.json` keep every field they had, and a reader that predates the judge tier sees exactly what it saw before. Judging the same run twice asks nothing — a trial whose latest judgment carries the same request identity is skipped unless `--rejudge`."},"527":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-93","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-judge","content":"A trial that errored is never judged: there is no answer to score, and it is reported as skipped rather than as a zero. A judge that could not produce a judgment exits the command non-zero even under `--no-fail`, because a missing measurement must not be reported as a score."},"528":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-94","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"Summarizes a completed run directory."},"529":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-95","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"Option"},"530":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-96","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"Description"},"531":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-97","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-report","content":"`--run-dir <DIR>`"},"532":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-98",