`fail_on_missing_agent` defaults to **true** — the CLI refuses to run against a missing agent unless you explicitly set it to `false`. Don't assume otherwise from older examples."},"2056":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-64","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"With no `checks` file configured, there is effectively no deterministic signal: a case passes purely on the agent process exiting `0`. Point `checks` at a real file once you want the suite to assert anything about *what* the agent did."},"2057":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-65","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"Real output against a working config (this one set `timeout_seconds = 120` and `fail_on_missing_agent = false`):"},"2058":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-66","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"(`parallel: 0` here just means \"unset\" in the table renderer — the runner still falls back to CPU core count.) A broken `checks.toml` fails validation immediately, e.g.:"},"2059":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-67","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"A prompts CSV missing a required column fails the same way:"},"2060":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-68","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"The suite loader (`aikit-evals::suite`) reads a header row with **required** columns `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger`, plus optional `tags` and `workspace_subdir`."},"2061":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-69","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Column"},"2062":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-70","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Required"},"2063":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-71","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Meaning"},"2064":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-72","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`id`"},"2065":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-73","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2066":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-74","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Non-empty identifier per row. Used for `--case`, artifact folder names, and reports."},"2067":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-75","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`prompt`"},"2068":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-76","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2069":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-77","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Text sent to the agent. Use CSV quoting (`\"...\"`, doubled `\"\"` for an embedded quote) for commas or newlines."},"2070":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-78","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`should_trigger`"},"2071":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-79","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2072":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-80","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`true`/`1` (case-insensitive `true`) or anything else counts as `false`. &#x2A;*See the callout below — this column does not affect pass/fail.**"},"2073":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-81","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`tags`"},"2074":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-82","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"no"},"2075":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-83","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Comma-separated tags inside the cell (e.g. `\"smoke,basic\"`). Used by `eval run --tag <name>`."},"2076":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-84","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`workspace_subdir`"},"2077":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-85","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"no"},"2078":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-86","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Relative path that becomes the agent's working directory for the case. Under the default isolation it is created **inside the case's scratch workspace**, with fixture files copied in from the same path under the project root; under `--no-isolation` it resolves directly under the project root. Empty or omitted → workspace root."},"2079":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-87","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Empty lines are skipped."},"2080":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-88","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"**`should_trigger` is inert.** The field's own doc comment in `aikit-evals&#x60; says it plainly: &#x2A;\"Whether the skill should trigger (documentation-only; checks.toml is authoritative for pass/fail).\"* No scorer reads it. The same global check list from `checks.toml` runs against **every** case regardless of what `should_trigger` says, and with no checks file configured, pass/fail comes only from the agent process's exit code. There is currently no way to express a per-case \"this prompt must NOT trigger the skill\" expectation — treat the column as documentation for a human reader, not as a control the CLI acts on. Do not build a suite on the assumption that setting `should_trigger,false` makes the suite verify non-triggering; it does not."},"2081":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-89","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"Point `checks` at a TOML file with one or more `[[check]]` tables, keyed by the required `name` field. There are exactly five check types (`aikit_evals::checks::CheckDefinition`):"},"2082":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-90","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"**Checks score the canonical trace, never raw stdout.** Every check below matches against the run's `trace.jsonl` — the parsed, structured event stream. Raw stdout is deliberately excluded: with the `claude` agent it opens with a `system`/`project init` event listing **every skill installed in the environment**, which used to make any skill-name pattern pass vacuously. Assistant text still reaches the trace as message events, so matching on what the agent actually said continues to work."},"2083":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-91","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"The check you almost certainly want for \"did my skill fire?\"."},"2084":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-92","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Field"},"2085":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-93","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Type"},"2086":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-94","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Required"},"2087":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-95","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Default"},"2088":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-96","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`skill`"},"2089":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-97","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"string"},"2090":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-98","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2091":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-99","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"— (omit to match *any* skill invocation)"},"2092":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-100","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`expected`"},"2093":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-101","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"bool"},"2094":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-102","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2095":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-103","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`true` (`false` asserts the skill did **not** run)"},"2096":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-104","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`required`"},"2097":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-105","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"bool"},"2098":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-106","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2099":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-107","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`true`"},"2100":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-108","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Matches a **structured `Skill` tool invocation** in the trace, not a substring of prose. When `skill` is given, it must **exactly equal** the invocation's skill-identifying input field (`skill`, `name`, or `skillName`) — `\"foo\"` does not match a `\"foo-bar\"` invocation, and a skill name merely mentioned in argument text does not count. This is the robust way to assert triggering — and, with `expected = false`, the only reliable way to assert non-triggering."},"2101":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-109","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Field"},"2102":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-110","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Type"},"2103":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-111","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Required"},"2104":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-112","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Default"},"2105":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-113","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`pattern`"},"2106":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-114","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"string"},"2107":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-115","pa