,"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#zero-step-runs","content":"A run that finishes without recording a single training step does **not** print the line\nabove. It prints a distinct message on stdout and a warning on stderr:"},"2609":{"id":"/optimize/running-15","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#zero-step-runs","content":"The usual cause is a suite with no `train` rows, which `optimization run` now rejects up front\nwith `OPTIMIZE_NO_TRAIN_CASES` (see Setup). This warning is the\nbackstop for every other way a run can end up doing nothing — for example a loop\nconfiguration that yields no steps. Treat it as a failed run, not a successful one:\n`best_skill.md` is the seed document, unchanged."},"2610":{"id":"/optimize/running-16","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#override-the-output-directory","content":"This overrides the `out_dir` value in the config without modifying the file."},"2611":{"id":"/optimize/running-17","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#disable-scoring-isolation","content":"Scoring passes are isolated by default (see the `isolate` knob in Configuration); `--no-isolation` scores in a shared workspace against the machine's ambient agent environment instead. The decision is persisted into the run's provenance `optimize.toml`, so a later `resume` keeps the same behaviour. Baselines recorded before isolation existed were measured against the ambient environment — expect gate and baseline scores to shift on the first isolated run."},"2612":{"id":"/optimize/running-18","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#resume-an-interrupted-run-in-one-step","content":"If you interrupted a run (Ctrl-C, timeout, machine restart), you can resume it directly from the `run` command:"},"2613":{"id":"/optimize/running-19","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#resume-an-interrupted-run-in-one-step","content":"This delegates to the `resume` subcommand — it re-reads the stored config from the run directory and picks up where it left off."},"2614":{"id":"/optimize/running-20","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#watch-progress-with-status","content":"In a second terminal, run:"},"2615":{"id":"/optimize/running-21","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#watch-progress-with-status","content":"This prints the current best score, epoch/step position, and a per-step table:"},"2616":{"id":"/optimize/running-22","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#watch-progress-with-status","content":"Column meanings:"},"2617":{"id":"/optimize/running-23","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#watch-progress-with-status","content":"Column"},"2618":{"id":"/optimize/running-24","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#watch-progress-with-status","content":"Description"},"2619":{"id":"/optimize/running-25","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#watch-progress-with-status","content":"`step`"},"2620":{"id":"/optimize/running-26","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#watch-progress-with-status","content":"Global step index, **0-based** across all epochs. This is the value to pass to `optimization inspect --step`."},"2621":{"id":"/optimize/running-27","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#watch-progress-with-status","content":"`gate`"},"2622":{"id":"/optimize/running-28","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/running#watch-progress-with-status","content":"Whether the patch was accepted or rejected."},"2623":{"id":"/optimize/running-29","page_id":"/optimize/running","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/ru