fest intent and locked origin differ."},"3160":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-28","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`revision-mismatch`"},"3161":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-29","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Installed and locked versions differ."},"3162":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-30","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`content-mismatch`"},"3163":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-31","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Installed managed content differs from its digest."},"3164":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-32","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`integrity-error`"},"3165":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-33","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Installed content could not be verified."},"3166":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-34","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`insufficient-integrity`"},"3167":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-35","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"The lock lacks evidence required for a reliable check."},"3168":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-36","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`ownership-conflict`"},"3169":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-37","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Bundle owners disagree about the expected content."},"3170":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-38","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`extraneous`"},"3171":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-39","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Installed content has no manifest, lock, bundle, or override owner."},"3172":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-40","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#json-schema","content":"Do not test a nonexistent `.status` field. Use `reconciliation` for reports and use the\n`--check` exit status for pass/fail automation."},"3173":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-41","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#group-scoped-checks","content":"`--only` and `--without` affect both displayed rows and the selected check closure. They are\nmutually exclusive."},"3174":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-42","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#group-scoped-checks","content":"The implicit group for an ungrouped root is `default`. `--only default` is valid even for an empty\nproject and produces an empty successful result."},"3175":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-43","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#ci-example","content":"The last command fails the step when reconciliation is required. Keep the JSON artifact for\ndiagnostics; no `jq` predicate is required to decide success."},"3176":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-44","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#ci-example","content":"For a readable failure report while preserving the command's exit status:"},"3177":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-45","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#repair-workflow","content":"Use the row status to choose the repair:"},"3178":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-46","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#repair-workflow","content":"fastskill refuses to overwrite locally modified managed content during update/removal. Preserve or\nrevert the local change before retrying. Editable installs are intentionally mutable and are checked\nby link shape rather than copied-content digest."},"3179":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-47","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#global-state","content":"Use `--global` to reconcile `global-skills.lock` and the global skills directory:"},"3180":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-48","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#global-state","content":"Global checks treat an extraneous on-disk skill as a reconciliation failure, matching project\nchecks."},"3181":{"id":"/skill-management/validation","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","type":"page","content":"Validate a skill","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Manage skills","Skills and projects"],"tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/validation"},"3182":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-0","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation","content":"Check skill structure and installed state before an agent uses it."},"3183":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-1","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"Start with SKILL.md"},"3184":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-2","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"Validate installation and state"},"3185":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-3","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"A skill root contains `SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter and instructions:"},"3186":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-4","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"The standard validator expects a lowercase name of 1–64 characters using letters,\ndigits, and single separating hyphens. The description must be nonempty and at most\n1024 characters. Name and description help an agent decide when to load the skill."},"3187":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-5","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"FastSkill derives identity from the skill metadata/name and uses a semantic version\nwhen resolving or packaging skills. Version metadata is optional for a minimal skill;\nFastSkill defaults an unspecified version to `1.0.0`. Set `metadata.version`\nexplicitly for a skill you distribute."},"3188":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-6","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"After creating the source above, add it from a configured project:"},"3189":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-7","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"Installation validates metadata and source contents. Reconciliation checks desired\nconstraints, locked facts, dependency ownership, and installed content. Editable\nlocal sources are reported as mutable rather than digest-verified."},"3190":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-8","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"A successful structural check does not prove that instructions are safe or useful.\nReview scripts and resources, then use evals to measure\nbehavior on representative tasks. See reconciliation\nfor missing, changed, conflicting, and unverifiable installations."},"3191":{"id":"/testing/debugging","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"page","content":"Debugging Guide","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Diagnostics"],"tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging"},"3192":{"id":"/testing/debugging-0","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging","content":"Diagnose FastSkill setup and behavior with `fastskill cli doctor` and `--verbose` output."},"3193":{"id":"/testing/debugging-1","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging#overview","content":"Overview"},"3194":{"id":"/testing/debugging-2","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`fastskill cli doctor`"},"3195":{"id":"/testing/debugging-3","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging#verbose-output","content":"Verbose output"},"3196":{"id":"/testing/debugging-4","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging#see-also","content":"See also"},"3197":{"id":"/testing/debugging-5","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#overview","conte