tions** (per case, then averaged across the split — see\nSetup):"],[2496,"**Gate metric**"],[681,"**Generates Skill ID**: Uses the current directory name as the skill ID"],[3008,"**Git marketplace**: a Git repository with a marketplace document."],[2869,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[2873,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[1246,"**git-marketplace**: Git repository with `marketplace.json` for skill discovery"],[294,"**Global lock**: `~/.config/fastskill/global-skills.lock` (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\fastskill\\global-skills.lock` (Windows)"],[1324,"**Grid**: Human-readable columnar layout with the same fields as table"],[3009,"**HTTP registry**: an HTTP index and downloadable skill artifacts."],[1250,"**http-registry**: HTTP-based registry with flat skill index"],[2800,"**ID** → Second directory level (the package name, must not contain slashes, e.g., \"web-scraper\")"],[2722,"**If you omit `checks` from `optimize.toml` entirely, there is no grading signal at all**: with zero checks configured, every case's result list is empty, and an empty list scores `1.0` under every `gate_metric` (vacuously — \"zero required checks passed\" is trivially true). In that configuration every candidate patch looks perfect, so the gate has nothing meaningful to accept or reject on. Always configure `checks` for a real run."],[2997,"**Include all metadata**: Provide tags, capabilities, and author information"],[2752,"**Incremental index rebuilding.** A change-detection cache (`.fastskill/build-cache.json`) lets\nFastSkill\nre-embed only what actually changed, so keeping the index current is cheap."],[1893,"**Index for search**: `fastskill index rebuild` (requires `OPENAI_API_KEY`)."],[1892,"**Install from the manifest**: `fastskill project install`."],[825,"**Installs Skills**: Stages and commits each overlapping dependency closure as one recovery unit"],[715,"**Invalid IDs:**"]